          'Row controls = ONE pinned column id "controls", header "Intake" (th/td sticky left-0, z-20/z-10, bg-white). Merges a "Status" column (really the intake toggle, and misread as open/filled/draft) + a separate Actions column that sat in position 7 and scrolled out of view. Intake toggle is jobs-view-only; the gear is NOT gated (it is the only route to Settings since the menu entry was removed, and the dashboard needs it). Toggle POSTs /hiring-jobs/setting/{uuid} {auto_import_candidates_from_ats}. The dashboard variant of the column keeps header "Actions" + enableSorting:false, since it has no toggle to sort.',
          'Intake dot states (utils/jobIntakeState.ts, unit-tested): paused = setting flag false, whatever the tournament does; live = flag true + active_tournament non-null (in-progress statuses created..create_assistant_id count as active); live_not_evaluating (half green/half grey) = flag true + active_tournament null. row.evaluation.uuid is NOT the signal, because evaluationTournamentOf falls back to tournaments[0], which can be archived; the mapper keeps evaluation.active from active_tournament instead. Pausing intake never stops the runner (it does not read the flag), so grey copy must not claim evaluation stops. Pause Evaluation was removed 2026-10-02 (one active tournament per job), so half has no other cause. Sort stays intake-only. On slider close, refreshSliderJobsIntake re-reads the intake flag of every job the slider showed (watch on jobViewData.job_id; the pager moves through several), one GET /hiring-jobs?lite=1&active=0&search=<uuid> each, since the slider Pause/Resume and starting a tournament both change it. It cannot ride on refreshLoadedEvaluations: that request keeps the Active only filter, so a job just paused in the slider is missing from it.',
          'Sorting on that column maps controls -> auto_import_candidates_from_ats (backend orderByRaw over the JSON setting; "status" is an accepted alias). It is a NO-OP whenever active=1, which is the default, so sortableHeader takes an optional title that may be a function -- read inside the render closure so it stays reactive -- and the Intake header uses it to say so rather than presenting an arrow that appears broken.',
          'FILTER GAP: HiringJobController line ~295 is `if ($active)`, truthy only. active=1 narrows via whereHas(setting flag true); active=0 applies NO filter. So the toolbar switch is on=active-only / off=ALL, and there is no paused-only view. Jobs with no hiring_job_settings row are excluded by active=1 AND render grey (mapper defaults the flag to false), so /jobs is self-consistent -- but the /hiring-jobs list endpoint computes is_active_job as `!$job->setting || flag`, i.e. the OPPOSITE default. Any paused-only filter must mean NOT-active, not flag===false.',
          'Candidates column = total_candidates_count, which is withCount over the job sources relation with NO filter. other_ats/resumes/linkedin/ext_recruiter are the same relation filtered by source, hence true subsets; the popover shows total-minus-named as "Other sources" so the parts reconcile. ats_applications_count counts the applications relation and is NOT part of that total -- it sits below a divider. Do not sum them.',
          'white_glove_candidates_count is hardcoded 0 in HiringJobResourceCollection and sorted with orderByRaw("0 {dir}"), so the column could never render or order anything; dropped from the UI while the field still ships.',
          'Column visibility: useUserViewSetting("jobs-columns") -> user_settings (unique user_id+name, value json-cast, owner from auth()->id()). Stores the CSV of HIDDEN ids so columns added later default to visible; "none" is the sentinel because save() refuses an empty string, and null means never-chosen -> DEFAULT_HIDDEN_COLUMNS from code. Seeded synchronously before the fetch, because the load path swallows failures. Saves are optimistic and log-only on failure. controls + job_title are not offered to the picker.',
          'Department cell prefers CompanyDepartment.abbreviation (uppercased) resolved from /company/departments by id, falling back to the department embedded on the job (now carrying abbreviation; the index eager load is department:id,name,abbreviation). Server sort uses COALESCE(NULLIF(abbreviation,\'\'), name) so the ordering matches the rendered text.',
          'Slider pager: JobView props pagerIndex/pagerTotal/pagerLoading + a navigate emit; opt-in, so the requisition drawer and the member/recruiter editors get nothing. Denominator is pagination.total, NOT items.length. Crossing the loaded edge awaits loadMore(); backwards never fetches (append-only from page 1). router.replace (not push) keeps history clean. Runs confirmDiscardWorkflowChanges. Arrow keys stand down inside input/textarea/select and any role=combobox|listbox|menu|textbox; the listener is on window, so a stacked overlay still needs its own guard.',
