          'Planner IndeedJobSyncPlanner builds the LIVE careers feed (not the 3 h cache), deleted jobs included. Company errors stop planning: invalid_environment, recruiter_workspace_is_not_an_employer, invalid_source_name, company_not_configured_for_sandbox, sandbox_source_in_production, posting_identity_conflict. Per job, first match: indeed_distribution_opt_out, job_deleted, indeed_job_opt_out, careers_disabled, careers_job_opt_out, job_expired, not_in_public_careers (covers paused intake); these conditions EXPIRE an accepted posting. Then IndeedJobMapper content rules: missing_* (uuid, title, requisition_id, description, country_code, city, apply_url, created_at), invalid_career_url, invalid_employer_email, invalid_employer_phone (company phone must be +E.164, so one bad phone blocks every job), missing_employer_identity, invalid_country_code, invalid_publication_date, invalid_description_length (< 100 visible chars or > 65000 bytes of HTML), unsupported_salary_unit (USD CAD EUR GBP AUD CHF JPY KWD; HOUR DAY WEEK MONTH YEAR MILE SHIFT), invalid_salary_range. Content errors NEVER expire a live posting. With apply on, intake_disabled / missing_apply_credentials / missing_indeed_apply_post_url / invalid_indeed_apply_post_url block publishing as well. The LinkedIn switch and the job poster are not consulted.',
