          'Sender name (2026-10): defaults to the CONNECTED ACCOUNT HOLDER (Google name, else given+family; Microsoft displayName, else givenName+surname), never the admin who connected it or the company. Set on each mailbox connect (EmailCalendarConnectService::applySenderNameOnConnect), provenance in meta.sender_name_source = profile | custom. A typed name survives reconnecting the SAME account (provider id, else address); another mailbox takes its own profile name; an automatic name refreshes on reconnect. Status returns EmailConnection::senderName() without writing, so older rows show the profile name with no reconnect. Google From = "<name>" <account_email> (GoogleConnectionService::fromHeader, RFC 2047). Microsoft: Exchange stamps the mailbox directory display name on Graph mail, so the name is read-only here and update() refuses it (422). That Microsoft behaviour comes from integrator docs, NOT yet a staging send.',
          'Room discovery on this card (dev plan 2026-11-01): behind MailboxRoomDiscoveryRollout, off until activation and pilot, so the published copy below stays conditional until then and changes at activation. Company, Google, slug email only; the room option and Enable, Reconnect and Stop live in the mailbox modal on /setting, whose deep link /setting?open=mailbox-room-discovery the Meeting Rooms page uses. Flow, consent evidence (meta.room_discovery_consent) and the callback rules: MailboxRoomDiscoveryFlow. See Meeting Rooms Directory.',
          'Reconnect keeps bookings (dev plan 2026-11-04, BookedMailbox): a booking belongs to its mailbox = recorded calendar owner company + provider + account address (trimmed, no case), never to the email_connections row. Disconnect deletes the row (EmailCalendarConnectService::removeConnection), so does Ivy after 4 rejected token refreshes (EmailConnection::REFRESH_TOKEN_FAILURE_DELETE_THRESHOLD), and the next Connect inserts a new id; stored connection ids stay as a record and are compared only for a row with no captured address. Three answers: same (proceed), none (owner has no full-access row), different. None: onsite Edit and Manual Schedule of a live event are refused mailbox_disconnected before anything is opened (never a new invite: needsNewInvite stays false, also afterwards); a change at its apply step fails mailbox_disconnected, nothing sent; a change whose answer was lost stays unknown and is read again; onsite creates and cancels go back to pending, not counted as an attempt, re-checked on the last backoff step (15 min) by the 5-minute reconciler with no reconnect signal; auto-schedule claims are left for the next run until the claimed meeting ends. Deadlines: a booking at the start of its first waiting meeting (then every waiting segment fails and the day goes incomplete, no partly elapsed day is finished without a person), a cleanup at its meeting\'s end (then a retriable failure with Retry cleanup). Different: edits fail connection_replaced, a readback fails connection_replaced_unconfirmed, cancels orphan, and Intro and Tech keep the documented new-invite path. Limitation: an address deleted and reissued to another account passes the check; changes then fail as missing, and cancels report false success, because providers treat a missing event as done. Disconnect confirmation (F4): the company mailbox\'s Disconnect first calls GET /company/oauth-integration/full-access-bookings?provider= (open to every member like the other status reads; delete-full-access stays company.role:admin), answered by MailboxUpcomingBookings with {connected, provider, onsite_days, interviews}. Onsite days: issue not cancelled/superseded, BookedMailbox SAME, with a created segment, cancel_status none, starting after now. Interviews: awaiting_meeting rows ahead, not onsite (onsite_plan_issue_id null), with a live event (event_id, no canceled_at/provider_cancel) at this provider and owner (calendar_owner_company_id, else the job\'s company); they record no address, so they count for whatever mailbox the owner has now. A failed count still shows the warning without numbers; personal connections disconnect at once (pages/setting/index.vue askToDisconnect, components/setting/MailboxDisconnectConfirm.vue, utils/mailboxDisconnectWarning.ts).',
