          'Availability: SharedCalendarAccessService::getBusyLookupsForRoomIds via the company FULL-ACCESS (AI Managed Mailbox) connection, addresses looked up from the company directory mirror, never client-supplied (would be a free/busy probe), so it needs no directory connection. Only addable rooms and rooms on this event are answered; any other id of the company is left out without a provider call (another company\'s id is still a 422 for the whole request). Circuit breaker consulted BEFORE calling. Since Rooms CAT-3a: Octopyd\'s own holds first (App\\Services\\Rooms\\RoomHolds, shared with the onsite planner: other active interviews, days being published, room steps still owed) make a room busy with reason held_in_octopyd even when its calendar cannot be read; a room on this event that has not declined is never busy because of this booking; a read that fails outright leaves held rooms busy and the rest unknown (temporary_provider_error); otherwise unknown carries the lookup\'s skipped_reason or status. Lookups are cached 60 s under the mailbox account and credentials_generation, so a reconnect never reuses the old answer. Microsoft: a getSchedule entry with no error and no scheduleItems is unknown, not free. No mailbox -> every room unknown. Half-open overlap. ADVISORY ONLY (R8): busy and unknown rooms stay selectable and the save reads none of it; Google and Microsoft auto-decline a taken room, and that RSVP is the real booking signal.',
