          'Candidate Guide in every stage state (2026-10-23, the user\'s request): Workflow.vue canEditStageGuide = canUpdate and, on a candidate journey, a stored configurable stage (savesStageGuideAlone) or canEditStage. Such a stage saves the guide alone and at once, Save guide in components/job/workflow/CandidateGuideModal.vue: PUT candidates/{candidate}/{job}/journey-stages/{stage}/guide (CandidateController::updateCandidateJourneyStageGuide; job authority as for the whole-plan save, Tech Lead past onsite refused by DenyTechLeadPostOnsiteMiddleware, intro / tech / onsite only, description_revision checked: 409 stage_conflict with their guide, shown in the modal with Use theirs). utils/stageGuide.ts takeStoredGuide puts the stored guide and only its revision on the stage and its baseline, so other unsaved edits stay. A stage not saved yet, and the job editor, keep the guide with Save journey / Save workflow. The whole-plan save still holds a booked or past stage to what is stored, guide included.',
          'Feedback & decision redesign "C" (2026-10-24, chosen by the user from the preview artifact THLoY9FgMUGHcN5zoKbVjY, read first, write on demand): whatever is written on a stage (notes, feedback, the final decision, and the interviewers still to write: decision_summary.pending_feedback_user_ids named by participant_roles, getPendingFeedbackPeople) shows in every phase to every viewer who may read it, in JourneyStageEntries.vue as an Interviewer feedback list and a Comments list. The comment line (JourneyQuietLine) and the hide-the-feedback toggle (stagePanelOpen, stageFeedbackHidden) are gone. Two cards since 2026-10-25 (the user\'s request): the read card, JourneyStageDecisionPanel.vue titled Comments & feedback (status, progress, Reopen Decision, the entries with each comment in a bordered box of its own, journey-stage-comment, "No feedback or comments yet."), shows on every interview stage whenever shouldShowStageActionPanel allows, in every phase, and folds to its header with its own chevron (local state: folded while nothing is written, comments, feedback or the decision, and open once something is, so a first comment opens it, until the viewer uses the chevron; folded it says "n feedback · n comments" or "No feedback or comments yet"); it has no write buttons (the header\'s Comment, Recommend and Decide are gone). Under it the write card, JourneyStageWriteCard.vue titled Feedback & decision (light gray, bg #F8F8F8 since 2026-10-25, the editor white; data-testid journey-stage-write-box), is hidden by default and shows only while it is open: Workflow.vue stageComposers (by stage id) holds {kind: feedback | note}, dropped once its note or decision is saved (persistStageNote, submitStageDecision). On an interview stage it is one box with every action the viewer has side by side, as before redesign "C": Reject at this stage, Recommend reject, Post comment, Recommend advance, Advance to <next stage> (utils/journeyStageComposer.ts stageWritingActions on utils/stageWritingRights.ts since stage decide S3a: Recommend for can_feedback, the outcome for can_decide, on any stage size and on an onsite for its deciders too); the outcome, else the vote, else the comment is the solid button. The read card\'s header shows getConsensusBadge (journey-consensus-badge) beside the status while every counted vote agrees and nothing is decided. It has the support text (getStageActionSupportText), the pre-schedule reason (vote or outcome rights, not while sensitive), JourneyStageComposer (sensitive-data box for a viewer who may comment, or while ticked), and an X to close. A sensitive draft disables the vote and the outcome (stageActionControlsBlocked); rejects go through RejectionReasonDropdown, except an onsite Recommend reject. Add feedback and decision (2026-10-23, the header toggle beside Interview plan / Day plan, aria-pressed while the write card is open) opens and closes the write card (kind note on Offer Letter / Hired, else feedback); from an hour before the booked interview starts (an onsite\'s first meeting) until a final decision is made, the write card is open by itself as if the button had been clicked, without taking the cursor, and again after a post (2026-10-29, the user\'s request, utils/journeyInterviewAssistant.ts isJourneyWriteCardDue; X closes it until the button opens it again; not before a time is booked; not inside the Interview Room); opening scrolls journey-stage-write-box into view with block nearest (only as far as needed, not at all when it shows; centring it hid the card\'s header on 2026-10-24) and focuses the composer with preventScroll (2026-10-25, the user\'s request). Offer Letter / Hired: JourneyStageNotesPanel.vue is the read card (notes always shown, folds with its chevron, no Add note); the write card writes the note (Save note). Only the current stage takes writing (CandidateJourneyStageResource::canAddNote / canOpenStageAction refuse others).',
