        summary: 'ARVO coordinates interview scheduling around the active candidate stage.',
        body: [
          'When a candidate reaches a schedulable stage, they receive or can be sent a scheduling email for that active stage. The candidate uses the scheduling page to choose an available time with the interviewer or interviewers assigned to that stage.',
          'For normal stage-entry scheduling, Ivy creates or reuses the interview record and schedules the candidate time-selection email with a short delay. Before sending, Ivy checks that the candidate is still in the same stage and that the interview is still awaiting candidate scheduling. Explicit resend and reschedule-request emails are sent immediately.',
          'The scheduling page can display days and slots in the candidate-selected viewer timezone, but booking submits the selected start and end as UTC. Ivy treats UTC as the source of truth and final-validates the selected window before creating the provider calendar event.',
          'The scheduling experience depends on interviewer availability rules, available free/busy calendar signals, company mailbox setup, stage duration, meeting format, and whether the stage is virtual or onsite. Candidates cannot book same-day under the current scheduling rules.',
          'If Ivy cannot fully verify hiring team calendar availability at booking time, the candidate should receive a clear message that the selected time has been received and that the hiring team will confirm the meeting or follow up with alternate times if needed.',
          'Once booking succeeds, Ivy creates the Google Meet or Microsoft Teams event from the AI Managed Mailbox, records the provider event id, scheduled time, meeting type, meeting link where available, and the relevant interviewer or interviewers, then sends the shared calendar invite.',
          'Successful interview bookings are recorded in the candidate Activity & Feedback timeline so the hiring team can see when a candidate selected an interview time.',
          'After the interview is scheduled and conducted, the interviewer or an authorized reviewer can leave stage-specific feedback, add comments, submit sensitive information, recommend an outcome, or make a stage decision when they have authority.',
        ],
        bullets: [
          'Availability settings include timezone, weekday toggles, work hours, buffers, minimum scheduling notice, inclusions, exclusions, and virtual or onsite overrides.',
          'The candidate is offered a time only with interviewers who are not on a company holiday then, and cannot book over a holiday. See Company Holiday Calendars.',
          'The next scheduling request is sent or exposed when the candidate advances to the next schedulable stage.',
          'The Candidate Journey tab shows whether a stage is waiting on candidate scheduling, scheduled, awaiting interviewer feedback, or finalized. It can also surface RSVP, reminders, and calendar health for scheduled interviews.',
          'When availability cannot be fully verified, the hiring team can confirm the meeting manually or cancel and request reschedule. RSVP monitoring cancels an Intro Call or Tech Interview when the candidate declines the invite, tells the hiring team without cancelling anything when the candidate declines a session of an onsite day booked as a whole day, and reacts when a required interviewer declines.',
          'Declining a calendar invite, cancelling an interview, and rejecting a candidate are three different things. An interviewer declining an invite means one person is not attending and cancels nothing. The candidate declining their invite cancels an Intro Call or Tech Interview, but never an onsite day booked as a whole day. Cancelling ends the booking. Rejecting is a hiring decision.',
          'On an onsite day made of several sessions, one interviewer declining the invite never cancels the day. Every session stays booked, the decline is shown against the person who made it, and the job\'s department head, main hiring manager, HR, and Tech Leads are notified once so someone can find a replacement. On a day booked by the hiring team, declines by optional participants are not acted on. The candidate declining the invite for a session cancels nothing either, on a day on one date or several and whichever side booked it: every session stays booked, and the same people are told once to ask the candidate what time works and move the session, or to cancel the day only if the candidate no longer plans to attend.  Declining only the lunch cancels nothing too, and the hiring team is told.  A day the candidate booked before onsite days had segments keeps the earlier rule: the candidate declining any session cancels every session of that day that has not started yet.',
          'Cancelling an onsite day cancels every session in it, and the calendar provider notifies each attendee about each meeting removed from their calendar. Whether Ivy also emails the candidate depends on how the day was cancelled; see When an Onsite Day Changes.',
          'Meeting times in Ivy should be shown in the hiring team member source-of-truth timezone when viewed by the hiring team, even if the candidate booked from a different timezone.',
        ],
