          'A meeting time is one fixed moment, and Ivy shows it in the time zone of the person looking at it. Your own times use the time zone saved in your profile, wherever you are. Every time carries a short label such as PST or MST. Hover, focus, or tap the label to see the location, the full time zone, the GMT offset, and the date.',
          'Labels follow the date of the meeting, not today. In the rules Ivy uses, a meeting on November 5, 2026 at 17:00 GMT is 9:00 AM PST in Los Angeles and 10:00 AM MST in Vancouver, because British Columbia stayed on the same clock year round from November 2026. A meeting on July 15, 2026 at 16:00 GMT is 9:00 AM PDT in both cities.',
