          'Request a different time, sent from the candidate\'s portal, never cancels anything on an onsite day. The booking stays as it is, and the job\'s department head, main hiring manager, HR, and Tech Leads receive an in-app notice and an email quoting the candidate\'s note. The request waits on the onsite card until someone acknowledges and resolves it, and moving the day\'s meetings with Edit resolves it by itself.',
          'Cancel the meeting, sent from the candidate\'s portal, cancels every session of the day that has not started and puts the stage back to Hiring Team Is Booking. The same people receive an email and an in-app notice with the candidate\'s note, and any open requests close.',
          'Calendar responses. An interviewer declining their session never cancels the day: it appears in the stage\'s queue as An interviewer declined their invite, and the authorities are told once per person. On a day booked by the hiring team, declines by optional participants are not acted on. The candidate declining only the lunch cancels nothing, and the authorities are told.  The candidate declining any other session cancels nothing either, on a day on one date or several and whichever side booked it: every session stays booked, the session shows the decline on the onsite card, and the stage\'s queue shows The candidate declined the calendar invite with Acknowledge and Resolve.  The authorities get one email and one notice in Ivy for the day, saying nothing has been cancelled and asking them to find out what time works for the candidate and move the session in Edit day, and to cancel the day only if the candidate no longer plans to attend.  A second declined session adds no second notice while the first is open.  It closes when someone resolves it, when the candidate accepts the invite after all, or when the day is cancelled; moving the session does not close it.  Ivy sends the candidate no email about their decline.  A day the candidate booked before onsite days had segments keeps the earlier rule: their decline of any session cancels every session that has not started, and the candidate receives the email described in Interview Cancelled After the Candidate Declines.',
