          'Backend 937bf340 + f1364b79, talent-panel d2bbffd + 7017626 (components/application/{StageMessageComposer, SchedulingActivity}.vue, composables/useSchedulingActivity.ts, pages/application/[id].vue; the button is v-if can_message inside the EXPANDED stage details, so it shows before any interview exists). Stages listed on the talent page: intro-call, tech-interview, onsite, offer-letter, hired. dev / staging only so far. Ivy renders it through the existing components/job/CandidateSchedulingNoteRow.vue with no Ivy commit: "<Name> (Candidate):", plain text, and the server label "Candidate message".',
          'POST /api/talent/applications/{uuid}/stages/{stageId}/messages (talent.stage.messages.store, throttle 20/min), body {message 1..150 Unicode characters after trim, client_request_id uuid} -> TalentStageMessageController -> CandidateStageMessageService (transaction + row lock on the stage). Same client_request_id with the same text returns the same row with already_sent true; different text -> 409. POST only, no edit or delete. Row = candidate_scheduling_notes kind message (CandidateSchedulingNote::KIND_MESSAGE, MAX_MESSAGE_LENGTH 150; request and cancellation notes keep 2000 server-side while the portal caps cancellation notes at 150), session_key message:<uuid>, interview / issue / request ids null. No migration.',
