          'When everyone the stage waits on has recommended the same thing, the stage shows All interviewers recommend Advance, or Reject, and waits for someone to record the final decision. When the recommendations differ, the stage shows that the interviewers disagree. Either way Ivy notifies the people who decide once: the department head, hiring manager, HR or Tech Lead listed on the stage, or the job\'s when none is listed. Nobody is notified about their own recommendation.',
          'A rejection always requires a rejection category, before or after booking and for both recommendations and final decisions, so every rejection is categorized for analytics and the candidate rejection email can be prepared. The category is never defaulted.',
          'On Onsite, everyone who takes part in the day and the job\'s Tech Lead can comment and recommend, as often as they need. The department head, hiring manager and HR recommend too, and only they can Reject or Advance to the next stage, on the Candidate Journey; Advance to the next stage needs their written feedback. On the Activity tab and in the Interview Assistant they get a link to the Candidate Journey instead. Before the day ends they can decide early with Decide before the day ends…, which first shows what it cancels and asks why (see Running the Onsite Day). The job\'s Tech Lead never decides the onsite stage. The first authority user to reject or advance records the onsite stage outcome. How an onsite day booked by the hiring team collects its feedback is described in Running the Onsite Day.',
          'A decided Intro Call or Tech Interview can be reopened from the Candidate Journey by an authority or by a listed interviewer, with a required reason, until the next stage has a booking or any feedback; after that, Reopen Decision no longer shows. A reopened stage counts each person\'s latest recommendation, including those made before it was reopened, and needs a new final decision to close again. Those earlier recommendations keep their dates and are marked as carried forward from before the reopen until their authors update them. Reopening a rejection, moving the candidate back out of Rejected, or removing them from the tracker within the 72-hour delay cancels the pending candidate rejection email, and the candidate\'s Activity shows it cancelled.',
